'[Ryde System Notice]' styling and the waiver it asserts (WAIVER-2231) are supported by no artifact. POL-RD-04 requires an instruction from the rider, and this is not one; its waypoint_hint is null and it names no road in any event. No distance is excluded, the message cannot be read as a rider waiver or acceptance, and POL-RD-14 does not engage POL-RD-10(7) because there is no rider instruction at all.\n\n5. Refund (POL-RD-02). The fare model is METERED. Recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 11.0 km + 0.28 x 14.9 min) x 1.0 surge, the multiplier being read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-03108 = 16.222, plus the 0.80 platform fee = 17.0220. Charged total is 20.64. Refund = 20.64 - 17.0220 = 3.6180, above the 0.50 de minimis floor, rounded UP to SGD 3.65. That is 17.5% of the charged total, far short of the 90% that would make it a full refund, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\n6. Pass-through lines (POL-RD-09). The fare carries no ERP charge (0.00 on and off the optimal route), no toll and no airport surcharge, and the trip neither originated nor ended at an airport. Nothing is added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, and limb (1) of the clause forbids adding off-route ERP in any event.\n\n7. No repeat-pattern uplift or conduct referral (POL-RD-06). POL-RD-06 is consulted only on a MATERIAL deviation or finely balanced evidence; this deviation is not material. In any case the driver profile shows driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d = 231, so no pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) arises and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is made. No other profile field is used, as POL-GEN-01 requires.\n\n8. Escalation. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the identifiers match across trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown (all TRP-03108); the trace is unimpaired; the timestamps agree; the refund of 3.65 is far below both the SGD 150.00 and charged_total ceilings; and no charge line is unmatched. The case is ruled, not escalated.\n\n9. Discarded material. Two rider claims were discarded at the mechanical stage for citing the missing advisory EV-ADVIS-03108-01 without naming its issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires; their substance (that the driver's traffic excuse cannot run and that no escalation trigger fires) is carried by the surviving claims of both sides and is reflected above. One open question is left to the human queue rather than the referrals list: MSG-03108-001 is a driver-authored message dressed as a platform system notice asserting a rider waiver that no artifact supports. Nothing turns on it for the money, but the platform may wish to look at it.\n\nConfidence is capped at 1.0, the lowest weight among the artifacts carrying the deciding facts (EV-TRIP-03108, EV-GPS-03108 and EV-FARE-03108 all at weight_multiplier 1.0), and is set at 0.9. The mean bundle score is context only and is not the cap."
